LABEL 2E0D Sub_FinishDefenderPatrolStartNew
COMMENT 2E0D <CCHUNK>
COMMENT 2E0D %%AUTOTITLE
COMMENT 2E0D Mark the entry of the Arr_DefendersData array immediately before the one
COMMENT 2E0D pointed to by Y as unused (by setting its location field to zero), and
COMMENT 2E0D launch a new patrol.  (The search for an available array slot is therefore
COMMENT 2E0D guaranteed to succeed because of the slot we just marked as free.)
COMMENT 2E0D ;;
COMMENT 2E0D This could be considered part of `Sub_MoveDefenderCheckHit`; its only use
COMMENT 2E0D is being tail-called from there.
COMMENT 2E0D
COMMENT 2E19 </CCHUNK>

LABEL 2E19 Sub_MoveDefenderCheckHit
COMMENT 2E19 <CCHUNK>
COMMENT 2E19 %%AUTOTITLE
COMMENT 2E19 Move one defender one step.  Check whether it collides with the player or
COMMENT 2E19 with a player's shot, and act accordingly if so — award points, and
COMMENT 2E19 initiate an explosion and sound effect.
COMMENT 2E19 ;;
COMMENT 2E19 On entry, data about defender being processed in registers:
COMMENT 2E19 .  B has struct[0] column idx
COMMENT 2E19 .  A has loc increment (from struct[1], $01 L-R / $FF R-L)
COMMENT 2E19 .  X has struct[2:3] location
COMMENT 2E19 .  U points to graphics data according to kind of defender
COMMENT 2E19 .  Y points just past struct of defender to be moved
COMMENT 2E19 .    (struct is one element of Arr_DefendersData)
COMMENT 2E19
COMMENT 2E1B
COMMENT 2E1B First call where this defender appears?  If so, skip
COMMENT 2E1B "hit check and erase" tasks.
COMMENT 2E22 $E1 = lower byte of $1F × $FF
COMMENT 2E28
DEC 2E29
COMMENT 2E2D
LABEL 2E39 MDCH_L01
COMMENT 2E3D
COMMENT 2E3D Defender intersects with some yellow; it got hit
COMMENT 2E40
COMMENT 2E40 Overwrite X value on stack with zero to signal this defender gone
CONST 2E41
COMMENT 2E45
COMMENT 2E47
COMMENT 2E47 Determine what kind of defender was destroyed
DEC 2E48
COMMENT 2E53
COMMENT 2E53 Special (red) defender destroyed
LABEL 2E53 MDCH_L02
DEC 2E57
COMMENT 2E5A
COMMENT 2E5A Normal (blue) defender destroyed
LABEL 2E5A MDCH_L03
COMMENT 2E5D
COMMENT 2E5D Tasks arising from destroyed defender
LABEL 2E5D MDCH_L04
COMMENT 2E68
COMMENT 2E68 Erase an 8-wide, 7-high block of pixels (i.e., 2 bytes wide), with the
COMMENT 2E68 top-left byte pointed to by X; this erases the defender
LABEL 2E68 MDCH_L05
CONST 2E69
LABEL 2E6B MDCH_L06
COMMENT 2E75
COMMENT 2E75 Retrieve location (X) and location/column increment (A); if this is an
COMMENT 2E75 active slot, compute new location
LABEL 2E75 MDCH_L07
CONST 2E78
COMMENT 2E80
COMMENT 2E80 A defender moving along the top row does so at double speed; update
COMMENT 2E80 location and increment in this case
COMMENT 2E88
COMMENT 2E88 Compute new column; if that takes the defender to or beyond the leftmost
COMMENT 2E88 column, or to one beyond the rightmost column, mark this patrol as over and
COMMENT 2E88 launch a new one
LABEL 2E88 MDCH_L08
COMMENT 2E98
COMMENT 2E98 Still on screen; store new location and column to the structure, and draw
COMMENT 2E98 defender in new position
DEC 2E9B
LABEL 2EA1 MDCH_L09
COMMENT 2EB2 </CCHUNK>

LABEL 2EB2 Arr_DefendersData
COMMENT 2EB2 <DCHUNK>
COMMENT 2EB2 %%AUTOTITLE
COMMENT 2EB2 %%RFD 4
COMMENT 2EB2 Array of 11 entries each of a four-byte structure:
COMMENT 2EB2 ;;
COMMENT 2EB2 .  byte - XColumn: $01 L-to-R; $1F R-to-L
COMMENT 2EB2 .  byte - KindAndVelocity: $01 L-R normal; $FF R-L normal; $41 L-R special
COMMENT 2EB2 .  word - Location
COMMENT 2EB2 ;;
COMMENT 2EB2 Initialised by code in Main_1a with both byte values $01 and all word
COMMENT 2EB2 values $0B3F.  So all structs are init'd to { $01, $01, (124, 41) }.
COMMENT 2EB2
HEX 2EB2-2EDD
LABEL 2EB4 Arr_DefendersData_Loc
COMMENT 2EDE </DCHUNK>

