LABEL 318E Sub_MovePlayerRight
COMMENT 318E <CCHUNK>
COMMENT 318E %%AUTOTITLE
COMMENT 318E Move the player right one half-byte, i.e., two pixels.  The condition for
COMMENT 318E no update to whole (whole + fraction == $1E) can in theory happen in two
COMMENT 318E ways: (whole, fraction) == ($1E, $00) or ($1F, $FF).  But the former will
COMMENT 318E always happen before the latter can become true, so the rightmost the
COMMENT 318E player can be is at ($1E, $00), i.e., in right-position with centre byte in
COMMENT 318E column $1E.
COMMENT 318E
COMMENT 318E If player already at right-end limit of travel...
COMMENT 3196 ....do not move (see comment above for detail)
COMMENT 3198
COMMENT 319B If toggling fraction results in new value being $00=right...
COMMENT 319E ....we can leave byte-column and screen-loc as they are
COMMENT 31A0 ....otherwise (new value $FF=left), increase byte-column and screen-loc
COMMENT 31A5
COMMENT 31A5 Other player movement subroutines jump here too
LABEL 31A5 MPR_L1
LABEL 31A8 MPR_L2
COMMENT 31A9 </CCHUNK>

LABEL 31A9 Sub_MovePlayerLeft
COMMENT 31A9 <CCHUNK>
COMMENT 31A9 %%AUTOTITLE
COMMENT 31A9 Move the player left one half-byte, i.e., two pixels.  The condition for no
COMMENT 31A9 update to whole (whole + fraction == $00) can in theory happen in two ways:
COMMENT 31A9 if (whole, fraction) == ($01, $FF) or ($00, $00).  But the former will
COMMENT 31A9 always happen before the latter can become true, so the leftmost the player
COMMENT 31A9 can be is at ($01, $FF), i.e., left-position, centre byte in column $01.
COMMENT 31A9
COMMENT 31A9 If player already at left-end limit of travel...
COMMENT 31AF ....do not move (see comment above for detail)
COMMENT 31B1
COMMENT 31B4 If toggling fraction results in new value being $FF=left...
COMMENT 31B7 ....we can leave byte-column and screen-loc as they are
COMMENT 31B9 ....otherwise (new value $00=right), decrease byte-column and screen-loc
COMMENT 31C0 </CCHUNK>

